  "findings": [
    "Gene selection and scaling: the 1.6.1 CSV loader with `view_configs` and the v2 `scaledGeneExpression` / `raw[mutations]` `gene_list` options select the same columns in the same order; the standardized expression agrees to the forward class (v2 scales in float32, 1.6.1 in float64). The 1.6.1 class default `view_configs` second entry (expression only) is the `expr` variant. The 1.6.1 methylation preprocessing (StandardScaler + PCA) has no v2 equivalent: `four_views` deviates.",
    "xgboost version: `subsample` and `colsample_bytree` below 1 draw from random_state, and the stream differs between xgboost 3.2.0 (v2 lock) and 3.4.1 (installed in the 1.6.1 venv; 1.6.1 only requires >=3.2.0). Identical float64 matrices and parameters give different trees on the two sides, so `expr_mut_sampling` and `preset` (subsample 0.8, colsample 0.6) are deviations here and `expr_mut` / `expr` run without sampling. A user moving between versions gets different seeded models.",
    "Default hyperparameters (B5): the 1.6.1 class defaults (no grid) are n_estimators=100, learning_rate=0.1, max_depth=6, subsample=0.8, colsample_bytree=0.8, reg_alpha=0, reg_lambda=1.0, random_state=42. The first grid point of hyperparameters.yaml (what a run uses) is max_depth=10, subsample=0.8, colsample_bytree=0.6, reg_alpha=0, reg_lambda=0.1 (grid: colsample 0.6/0.8, reg_alpha 0/1), on the view_configs expression+mutations. The working-tree v2 `xgboost` predictor defaults and the `MultiViewXGBoost` preset equal that grid point (`preset` variant: identical effective parameters, identical trees when the xgboost versions agree). reg_lambda is now a public hyperparameter, so every grid value is expressible; n_jobs is fixed to -1 in v2.",
    "Verified outside the committed run: with xgboost 3.2.0 installed on the 1.6.1 side as well (`uv pip install --target DIR xgboost==3.2.0`, `PYTHONPATH=DIR`), `expr_mut_sampling` and `preset` give bitwise identical predictions and feature importances (maximum difference 0.0). The `forward` tolerance of the importances is for the float32 gain statistics, which differ by 3e-8 between the two xgboost versions."
  ],
